{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact DX-T1 head 0b72dffc4a90fd3acd6c351cdd3cd483fb8a4fcd on builder/typed-define-t1-20261109, tree a7af981d, all 46 artifacts, for request 00c50371 under promise b1c862b2 and review request 1f0b3e07. The new package `@generalbusiness/dap-define` composes typed declarations into plain data. Lending and Counter now author their definitions through it, and the retained JSON and pins stay byte-identical. The head follows rulings 92c1bf71, 75cea6c4 and 0a797a2e.\n\nWhat I checked in the source:\n\n- The package. `packages/define/src/index.ts` builds plain objects for each item, act, guard, effect and send. Operands stay data. Grant and reason names, element member keys and field types exist only in the type checker. Two values travel outside the data: an inline rule's expression, on a non-enumerable symbol of its guard, and a definition's declared grants, reasons and diagnostics, on a non-enumerable symbol of the definition. `normalize` copies each row with object spread, which keeps neither symbol. Act names live in a module-private WeakMap, so no symbol reaches a normalized act. That is the gate 2 repair, and the metadata case now checks recursive symbol absence and the bounded JSON admission.\n- The compiler. `compile` normalizes, then reports rule findings, undeclared grants, undeclared refusal reasons and every validator problem, each with its act, form path and offending value. It throws `CompileError` before it returns any definition. It returns the per-act refusal list beside the definition and digest.\n- The runtime values. `lending` and `countingCommitments` are `normalize` of the authored source, evaluated once at import. Each application test compares that value with its retained JSON by deep equality and by canonical bytes, and checks the digest against the pin. `pins.test.ts` compiles both sources and compares them with the JSON. The Workers still read the JSON, and no Worker source imports the package. Counter's application browser entry, `apps/counter/browser/main.ts`, imports `countingCommitments` and so bundles the package. All 56 Counting cases at gate 3 ran that browser code.\n- `ruleReferences`. It parses through the same `compile` that `admit` calls, so a refused source gets the same refusal. The derive test asserts that for three sources, along with the quoted-text case of ruling 75cea6c4. It walks the admitted tree, returns two lists of names, and evaluates nothing. The profile's depth check bounds the walk. `findings` uses it and no longer scans rule text with a regex.\n- Element members. `ElemOf` maps a record element's declared members, except `self`, and keeps `row.self` as the whole element. `elementMember(row, name)` accepts any declared key, including `self`, through a phantom key type. Scalar and unannotated elements expose only `self`. This matches item 1 of ruling 75cea6c4.\n- The pins. I ran `scripts/check-definition-pins.mjs` on my own extracted copy of the head, outside the builder's worktree, with the head's own workspace packages. It exits 0 in check mode and writes nothing. It prints Lending `sha256:0c43dd56…` and Counter `sha256:b5582434…`, the pin the request names. `definition.json`, `commitments.json`, `pin.ts` and `commitments-pin.ts` do not change in this head.\n- The release plan. `scripts/public-release.json` adds `define` as the ninth package with three coordinated dependencies, and Git's source-only `./diff` export joins the exclusion tables. The guide and the note each state in one sentence that the compiled-output check and publication have not run, as ruling 0a797a2e asks.\n- The guide. The new section gives the six patterns, the four forms, the attribute effect's two subjects, and the pin-check command. It links the vocabulary page and does not copy it. Every added prose line is at most 79 characters.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. Main 64be0cab is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against main, the head changes exactly the 46 paths that its 46 artifacts cover. The commit-message check passes: 16 checked, 0 flagged. The lockfile adds only the workspace link and the package entry. No Wrangler, Worker, definition, pin or scenario file changes.\n- The gate. I read gate.exit at 8b7de735, tree 40556767: \"exit 0\". The launcher and driver exits read 0 too. The reconciliation records Node 150, Counting 56, Plain 4,051 plus one skip, and Native 1,133 plus two skips, 5,390 passes in all, with all six Scale cases. The gate's new `def-pins` step passed. Gates 1 and 2 stay recorded as failed. After gate 3, only the note, the gate 3 manifest and the guide's line wrapping change. The guide keeps the same words.\n- The evidence. The eight manifests hash to the values the note cites. Their 35 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match. The `scale.exit` of 1 inside the gate directory is scratch output that `scripts/scale-selection.test.mjs` captures on purpose, not a gate result.\n- The browser. Page run 42731853327 succeeded at 8178fe63. The note carries it to the head by input equivalence, not by a new run.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The package sits above bytes, contract and derive, and nothing below it imports it. The pinned JSON stays the unit of trust. Authored code produces it, and the gate's pin check and the application tests hold the two together.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The package runs at authoring time and in client bundles. It grants no authority, and the scope still judges the pinned bytes. `ruleReferences` only reads an admitted tree. The act-name repair keeps symbol-keyed metadata out of the data that bounded JSON admission reads.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes:\n\n- `normalize` walks every form kind by hand, about 85 lines, and duplicates the validator's knowledge of form shapes. A new form needs a case in both places until K-spell makes the canonical spelling exact.\n- Request item 4 asks for a CI check. The pin check runs as the gate's `def-pins` step and in `pins.test.ts`. No GitHub workflow runs it. If the planner wants that check on every push, a later head can add it.\n\nNo setting changes, and the hosted Workers judge the same pinned bytes. The planner decides whether this landing needs a deployment. This approval authorizes no deployment, publication or live acceptance. K-spell 2ad35350, DX-T3 f682cbc4 and DX-T4 d49269fd stay open.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b11a73beec235eb45188aff5f805d754b55db994","binding":"assigned","head":"0b72dffc4a90fd3acd6c351cdd3cd483fb8a4fcd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0bb41dca5c3a3efe3d2854cddfe106f2b86ed3e8\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b1c862b21b52ec13aacd209a09c0196d1dc194ea\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0bb41dca5c3a3efe3d2854cddfe106f2b86ed3e8","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}